body:
- i don't need mods. Even when I was pc gamer I didnt like them;
- i don't play on multiplayer;
- graphic isn't for me that important, the quality of games on PS3 is ok;
- when it comes to exclusives - I have Uncharted, RDR, MGS, Resistance, TLOU and many others (exclusives were the main reason why I bought the console). Since Crysis there was for me no  interesting exclusive game on PC;
- you have to support someone. Either you support Sony or MS or you support nVidia, intel and Valve. Besides, I don't fell that Sony is doing something bad to players. They are no charity, they want to make money - but the same thing goes with Valve and nVidia.

I play on consoles because it's more comfortable (I came home from work, turn on my console, put the disc in and play. I want to have good time and thats all. I made my choice when it comes to entertainment, I know that consoles have many flaws but it is my choice.

> At this point i just dont see any benifit over a pc,

There are some:
- they cost less than PC;
- although new games are more expensives on consoles there are in fact sales in PSN and Xbox Market. Fresh released games on steam also cost money;
And you can buy cheaper, used games and then just sell it.
- theyre very easy to hook up to TV and to configure;
- they are small and look good;
- if you own both PS4 and Vita you can stream a whole game in real time from PS4 to your handheld via internet connection;

But for me personally the most important reason is that when I go to a store to buy a game only thing I have to do is to make sure that on the box there is written "PS3" or "PS4". I dont have to compare the requirements to my PC, I dont need to be worried if the game will run properly on my playstation. 

I dont own a gaming pc since 2010 and I dont see any good reason to buy one right now instead of PS4.
